      {
        "id": 206878,
        "name": "Sonvar",
        "username": "Powerhound_2000",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/powerhound_2000/{size}/1859_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-11-06T16:41:53.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"bobbertoriley\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/bobbertoriley/48/1910_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> bobbertoriley:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The big feature that I'd like to see is to be able to re-roll with randomize but lock in certain decks/numbers so that they stay the same.&nbsp;For example, being able to say that (H)=4, or that I want to play against Citizen Dawn with The Naturalist as one of the heroes, but don't care what else comes up.&nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>You can do this already. &nbsp;If you don’t like what you got the first randomize remove the elements you didn’t like and click Randomize again. &nbsp;As long as you have less than three heroes it will maintain everything else.&nbsp;</p>",
