      {
        "id": 206881,
        "name": "NinjaMonkey",
        "username": "NinjaMonkey",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/n/67e7ee/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2017-11-07T14:10:07.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I'd second(third?50th?) the lock a hero/villain/environment option during randomization. The current randomization workaround just isn't intuitive nor user friendly nor, honestly, a very good one. Why not just add a Lock/Unlock button and just randomize those items not flagged as locked? Seems like it'd be just as easy as well to add an \"H\" setting, default to 4 (the mid-point),&nbsp;so the user can select the total number of heroes they want.</p><p>I know this thread isn't about mechanics changes, but I would really love the ability to add custom decks *cough*Cauldron*cough*. That is a kickstarter that needs to happen.</p>",
        "post_number": 26,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:36:26.854Z",
