      {
        "id": 206883,
        "name": "Killswitch",
        "username": "Killswitch",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/killswitch/{size}/2116_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-11-07T17:52:45.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"NinjaMonkey\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/n/67e7ee/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> NinjaMonkey:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I know this thread isn't about mechanics changes, but I would really love the ability to add custom decks <em>cough</em>Cauldron<em>cough</em>. That is a kickstarter that needs to happen.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I don't know if that will ever happen. It's not just about dragging and dropping artwork and text, Handelabra has to code the card interactions/rulings, as well as all of the art elements outside of the hero's deck. So basically, the only way I'd see it happening is if we were allowed to implement mods, and the community would have to do it from scratch.</p>\n<p>I believe the only way to play with Cauldron decks is through Tabletop Simulator.</p>",
