      {
        "id": 206885,
        "name": "NinjaMonkey",
        "username": "NinjaMonkey",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/n/67e7ee/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2017-11-07T18:20:21.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Killswitch\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/killswitch/48/2116_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Killswitch:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>NinjaMonkey wrote:</b><br><blockquote>I know this thread isn't about mechanics changes, but I would really love the ability to add custom decks *cough*Cauldron*cough*. That is a kickstarter that needs to happen.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nI don't know if that will ever happen. It's not just about dragging and dropping artwork and text, Handelabra has to code the card interactions/rulings, as well as all of the art elements outside of the hero's deck. So basically, the only way I'd see it happening is if we were allowed to implement mods, and the community would have to do it from scratch.I believe the only way to play with Cauldron decks is through Tabletop Simulator.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Or analog if you have the physical cards. I've played a bit with Tabletop Simulator. Even began work on scripting the Cauldron cards specifically to try and automate as much of the book-keeping&nbsp;as possible. I'm still no where near done though.</p>\n<p>I understand the complexities of what I'm asking. There's no way it could be something as simple as drap and drop. I'd imagine it would need to be a set of APIs, and a means to bundle completed decks and import them into the game. Not simple, and maybe not doable. But it would be nice.</p>",
        "post_number": 30,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:36:27.128Z",
